The issue: the space in `"C3 "` at position 2 is a real character that should appear in the output. But `rstrip()` strips it. The rule says "don't pad to the right" — meaning we shouldn't ADD trailing spaces, but we should KEEP spaces that are actual input characters.

The key insight: we should only strip trailing spaces that were added as padding (i.e., where the source line was shorter than the column index). Spaces that came from actual input characters must be preserved.
